     1	//! `WorkbookSession` — the owning, single-writer engine session (Phase 6.1B inc.2).
     2	//!
     3	//! This is the *implementation* of the binding-neutral [`EngineSession`] contract
     4	//! (`crates/ql-session`, the 6.1A Codex-validated spec at `docs/api/session-api.md`).
     5	//! Where the `ql-session` crate is the type-level contract, this is the concrete
     6	//! struct that **owns** the engine state — `Workbook + OpLog + CalcgraphSession +
     7	//! PlanCache + FunctionRegistry` — and threads a per-edit [`WorkbookRuntime`]
     8	//! through it so no borrow crosses an FFI boundary (GAP-PS-09; the
     9	//! `calcgraph_session.rs:69-71` "absorb into ONE owning struct" anticipation).
    10	//!
    11	//! ## Scope (6.1B inc.2 — core path + read/structure/table + snapshot_delta)
    12	//!
    13	//! Shipped **real**:
    14	//! - lifecycle (`new`/`close`/state gating, the `Busy` state, version `epoch`),
    15	//! - single-cell mutations (`set_value`/`set_formula`/`clear`/`set_format`/
    16	//!   `register_format`/`validate_formula`) + sheet `add`/`rename`/`delete`/
    17	//!   `restore`/`move` + `set_name` + table ops (`create`/`rename`/
    18	//!   `rename_column`/`resize`/`drop`),
    19	//! - recalc (`recalc_dirty`/`recalc_all`/`mark_volatiles_dirty`) under the
    20	//!   `Busy` + operation-registry model,
    21	//! - the read path (`snapshot`/`cell`/`list_sheets`/`query_range`) + the
    22	//!   `{epoch, state_seq}` version token + **`snapshot_delta`** (inc.2c-3 —
    23	//!   change-log design (a)),
    24	//! - operations + events (`cancel`/`operation_status`/`poll_events`).
    25	//!
    26	//! `batch` (inc.2c-4) + the multi-call **transaction handle** (`begin_transaction`/
    27	//! `txn_add`/`commit_transaction`/`rollback_transaction`, inc.2c-5 — a pure
    28	//! `SessionOp` buffer that commits through the same `batch` machinery) +
    29	//! **`undo`/`redo`** (inc.2c-7) + **`.qbook` `open`/`save`** (inc.2c-9 — Option 1:
    30	//! reconstruct from the envelope, fresh op-log/undo history) + **xlsx `import`**
    31	//! (inc.2c-10 — same Option-1 adoption, via `ql_io_xlsx` + the injected
    32	//! `EngineXlsxRecomputer`) + **`csv` `import`/`export`** (inc.2c-11 — via the
    33	//! pure-I/O `ql_io_csv`; no recompute since CSV has no formulas) are also real.
    34	//! **xlsx `export`** (inc.2c-12 — whole-workbook, via `ql_io_xlsx` behind the
    35	//! `xlsx-write` feature so the default reader-only build stays lean; without
    36	//! the feature it returns the honest `Capability` error) is also real. The
    37	//! remaining contract methods return a **surfaced** `Capability` /
    38	//! `not_implemented_in_v1_core` error (NOT a silent fallback — project
    39	//! No-Fallbacks rule) and land in later sub-increments:
    40	//! - function registration (6.4), reserved bulk ops (6.4/6.5).
    41	//!
    42	//! ## Two design facts that shape this increment
    43	//!
    44	//! 1. **Version token = `{epoch, state_seq}` (inc.2c-3 — F1/F2).** `state_seq` is
    45	//!    a session-owned monotonic clock that advances on every committed mutation
    46	//!    AND every recompute that changed ≥1 cell. It **replaces `oplog.len()`** as
    47	//!    the token's counter because `oplog.len()` does NOT advance on recompute
    48	//!    (`put_computed_at` appends no ops), which would let two distinct visible
    49	//!    states share a token and make `snapshot_delta` silently under-report.
    50	//!    (Historical note: pre-F2, a `set_value(Blank)` clear also appended no op
    51	//!    — that gap is now closed by `Op::ClearValue`, but the recompute case
    52	//!    remains the load-bearing reason `state_seq` exists.) `ql-oplog::OpLog`
    53	//!    DOES expose a
    54	//!    Loro VV (`oplog_vv()`), reserved for the v1.5 collab delta-sync path; the
    55	//!    opaque 24-byte token shape is unchanged (only the counter's meaning is).
    56	//!    `snapshot_delta` walks a bounded change-log keyed by `state_seq`; the
    57	//!    `epoch` (bumped on reorder/restore/table-op/undo) forces a full rebuild for
    58	//!    states the delta DTO cannot incrementally express.
    59	//!
    60	//! 2. **`EngineError` cannot have `From<RuntimeError>`** — orphan rules forbid
    61	//!    `impl From<LocalErr> for ForeignErr` when the foreign type is `Self`
    62	//!    (`EngineError` is from `ql-session`). So the Appendix-A mapping lives as
    63	//!    the free function [`map_runtime_err`] in this owning layer, not as a
    64	//!    `From` impl.
    65	//!
    66	//! ## Read-path enumeration note
    67	//!
    68	//! `snapshot` enumerates a sheet's populated cells from the live `Workbook`'s
    69	//! **overlay** entries (user + computed) ∪ formula cells ∪ format-overlay cells.
    70	//! This is complete for every session constructible in this increment: all
    71	//! cell data arrives via `WorkbookRuntime` mutators, which write to the column
    72	//! *overlays* (never the Arrow *base* chunks). Base chunks are only populated
    73	//! by bulk construction / import (`open`/`import` — surfaced-not-yet here), so
    74	//! base-chunk enumeration is a tracked follow-up that lands with `import`.
    75	
