  1198	    /// op-log + undo history (`baseline = loaded workbook`), so the undo
  1199	    /// invariant `baseline + replay(oplog) == workbook` holds trivially (the
  1200	    /// loaded workbook IS the baseline; replay of the empty log is identity) —
  1201	    /// matching `from_workbook` and avoiding Option 2's data-loss bug class
  1202	    /// (a loaded `oplog` whose replay diverges from the loaded envelope). The
  1203	    /// loaded file's op-log history is therefore NOT carried forward: a later
  1204	    /// `save` writes only THIS session's edits, and undo cannot cross the open
  1205	    /// point (the intended semantic). The on-disk `oplog.bin` is still loaded
