    30	/// eval layer ([`crate::scalar::dispatch_udf`]) stays decoupled from the session
    31	/// DTOs; the owning [`crate::session::WorkbookSession`] converts it to a
    32	/// `ql_session::dto::Diagnostic` (severity `Error`) and emits an
    33	/// `Event::CellDiagnostic` when it drains the per-recompute collector. The cell
    34	/// VALUE is unchanged (still `#CALC!`/`#TIMEOUT!`); this is purely additive so a
    35	/// failed UDF explains *why* (exit test 7). `code` is a stable `&'static str`
    36	/// (`udf_no_worker` / `udf_raised` / `udf_timeout` / `udf_worker_died` /
