   205	    /// range). `None` for paths without cell context (legacy callers,
   206	    /// tests).
   207	    formula_cell: Option<ql_types::Address>,
   208	    /// **6.4-3c (2026-05-29):** borrowed handle to the session's Python-UDF
   209	    /// worker, threaded in by the value-computing recompute / set_formula env
   210	    /// sites (`workbook_runtime`). `None` for the binding-only / validate paths
   211	    /// and for every legacy caller (`new` / `with_formula_cell`). Surfaced to
   212	    /// the dispatch site via the `CellEnv::udf_worker` override below.
   213	    udf_worker: Option<&'w RefCell<Box<dyn UdfWorker + Send>>>,
   214	    /// **6.4-3d (2026-05-29; megaudit blocker G):** borrowed per-recompute
   215	    /// collector the UDF dispatch site pushes a [`UdfCellDiagnostic`] into on a
   216	    /// failed (or no-worker) `=MYUDF(..)`. `None` for every path without a
   217	    /// session-owned collector (legacy ctors, `validate`, standalone txn). The
   218	    /// session lends `&self.udf_diagnostics` and drains it into
   219	    /// `Event::CellDiagnostic` after the runtime borrow ends. Interior-mutable
   220	    /// + `!Sync` like `udf_worker`; sound under single-threaded recompute.
   221	    udf_diagnostics: Option<&'w RefCell<Vec<UdfCellDiagnostic>>>,
   222	    /// **6.4B (item H):** the operation-level UDF time-budget deadline for the
   223	    /// recompute pass this env belongs to. `None` everywhere except the
   224	    /// value-computing recompute pass, which sets it via [`WorkbookEnv::with_op_deadline`]
   225	    /// from the runtime's pass-start deadline. Surfaced to the dispatch site through
